messages.content:
Thanks for sharing the code. The drawer becomes unresponsive because the GlassDrawer component stays mounted after closing, and its top-level container still intercepts touches. Reading overlayOpacity.value in render doesn’t trigger unmounting when the close animation finishes.

Fix summary
- Add a mounted state to unmount the drawer shortly after the close animation.
- Set pointerEvents on the top container so it never blocks touches when closed.
- Keep the overlay limited to the area to the right of the drawer.
- Lower blur intensity (especially on Android) to reduce lag and the “white ghost” feel.

Here’s a safe, drop-in replacement for your GlassDrawer. Save it exactly at src/components/GlassDrawer.tsx and keep HomeScreen as-is.

```typescript name=src/components/GlassDrawer.tsx
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import {
  View,
  Text,
  StyleSheet,
  TouchableOpacity,
  Dimensions,
  Platform,
  useColorScheme,
  Pressable,
} from 'react-native';
import { BlurView } from 'expo-blur';
import { LinearGradient } from 'expo-linear-gradient';
import { Feather } from '@expo/vector-icons';
import Animated, {
  useSharedValue,
  useAnimatedStyle,
  withSpring,
  withTiming,
  interpolate,
  Extrapolate,
} from 'react-native-reanimated';
import { getColors, spacing } from '../theme/designTokens';
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

const { width: SCREEN_WIDTH, height: SCREEN_HEIGHT } = Dimensions.get('window');

type Props = {
  isOpen: boolean;
  onClose: () => void;
  onNavigate?: (screen: string) => void;
  widthPercent?: number; // default 0.6 (60% width)
  blurIntensityIOS?: number;
  blurIntensityAndroid?: number;
  tint?: 'light' | 'dark' | 'default';
};

const GlassDrawer: React.FC<Props> = ({
  isOpen,
  onClose,
  onNavigate,
  widthPercent = 0.6,
  blurIntensityIOS = 70,       // slightly reduced to feel lighter
  blurIntensityAndroid = 22,   // lower for performance on Android
  tint = 'default',
}) => {
  const colorScheme = useColorScheme();
  const isDark = colorScheme === 'dark';
  const colors = getColors?.(!!isDark) ?? {
    text: isDark ? '#fff' : '#111',
    muted: isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.7)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.5)',
  };

  const DRAWER_WIDTH = Math.round(SCREEN_WIDTH * widthPercent);

  // Mounted gate to fully unmount after close animation finishes
  const [mounted, setMounted] = useState<boolean>(isOpen);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (isOpen) {
      setMounted(true);
      return;
    }
    const t = setTimeout(() => setMounted(false), 260); // match close timing
    return () => clearTimeout(t);
  }, [isOpen]);

  // reanimated shared values
  const translateX = useSharedValue(-DRAWER_WIDTH); // start off-screen to the left
  const overlayOpacity = useSharedValue(0);
  const contentScale = useSharedValue(0.98);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (isOpen) {
      // open
      translateX.value = withSpring(0, { damping: 20, stiffness: 100, mass: 0.8 });
      overlayOpacity.value = withTiming(1, { duration: 260 });
      contentScale.value = withTiming(1, { duration: 260 });
    } else {
      // close
      translateX.value = withSpring(-DRAWER_WIDTH, { damping: 20, stiffness: 120, mass: 0.8 });
      overlayOpacity.value = withTiming(0, { duration: 220 });
      contentScale.value = withTiming(0.98, { duration: 220 });
    }
  }, [isOpen, DRAWER_WIDTH, translateX, overlayOpacity, contentScale]);

  const drawerStyle = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({
    transform: [{ translateX: translateX.value }],
  }));

  const overlayStyle = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({
    opacity: overlayOpacity.value,
  }));

  // subtle parallax effect for interior content (optional)
  const innerScaleStyle = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({
    transform: [{ scale: interpolate(contentScale.value, [0.98, 1], [0.995, 1], Extrapolate.CLAMP) }],
  }));

  const handleNavigate = (screen: string) => {
    onClose(); // close first
    setTimeout(() => onNavigate?.(screen), 260);
  };

  if (!mounted) {
    // fully unmounted when closed — nothing to block touches
    return null;
  }

  const blurIntensity = Platform.OS === 'ios' ? blurIntensityIOS : blurIntensityAndroid;
  const blurTint = tint === 'default' ? (isDark ? 'dark' : 'light') : tint;

  const menuItems = [
    { id: 'home', label: 'Home', icon: 'home', screen: 'Home' },
    { id: 'profile', label: 'Profile', icon: 'user', screen: 'Profile' },
    { id: 'settings', label: 'Settings', icon: 'settings', screen: 'Settings' },
    { id: 'about', label: 'About', icon: 'info', screen: 'About' },
  ];

  return (
    <Animated.View
      style={[styles.container, { zIndex: 9999 }]}
      // critical: when closed, do not intercept touches
      pointerEvents={isOpen ? 'auto' : 'none'}
    >
      {/* Overlay: only covers the area to the RIGHT of the drawer */}
      <Pressable
        style={[StyleSheet.absoluteFill, { left: DRAWER_WIDTH }]}
        onPress={onClose}
        pointerEvents={isOpen ? 'auto' : 'none'}
      >
        <Animated.View
          style={[
            styles.overlay,
            overlayStyle,
            { zIndex: 10000, backgroundColor: isDark ? 'rgba(0,0,0,0.55)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.45)' },
          ]}
        />
      </Pressable>

      {/* Drawer surface (ensure it sits above the overlay) */}
      <Animated.View
        style={[
          styles.drawer,
          drawerStyle,
          {
            width: DRAWER_WIDTH,
            height: SCREEN_HEIGHT,
            left: 0,
            zIndex: 10001,
            shadowColor: '#000',
            shadowOpacity: isDark ? 0.5 : 0.28,
            shadowOffset: { width: 4, height: 0 },
            shadowRadius: 18,
            elevation: 28,
          },
        ]}
      >
        <BlurView intensity={blurIntensity} tint={blurTint} style={styles.blurContainer}>
          <LinearGradient
            colors={
              isDark
                ? ['rgba(25,25,25,0.78)', 'rgba(18,18,18,0.90)']
                : ['rgba(255,255,255,0.68)', 'rgba(245,245,245,0.82)'] // tone down for less "white ghost"
            }
            start={{ x: 0, y: 0 }}
            end={{ x: 0, y: 1 }}
            style={styles.gradientOverlay}
          >
            <SafeAreaView edges={['top', 'left', 'bottom']} style={styles.safe}>
              <Animated.View style={[styles.innerContent, innerScaleStyle]}>
                {/* Header */}
                <View style={styles.header}>
                  <Text style={[styles.headerTitle, { color: colors.text }]}>Menu</Text>
                  <TouchableOpacity
                    onPress={onClose}
                    style={styles.closeButton}
                    accessibilityLabel="Close menu"
                    accessibilityRole="button"
                  >
                    <Feather name="x" size={22} color={colors.text} />
                  </TouchableOpacity>
                </View>

                {/* Items */}
                <View style={styles.menuItems}>
                  {menuItems.map((item) => (
                    <TouchableOpacity
                      key={item.id}
                      style={{
                        marginBottom: spacing.sm,
                        borderRadius: 14,
                        shadowColor: '#000',
                        shadowOffset: { width: 0, height: 4 },
                        shadowOpacity: isDark ? 0.35 : 0.08,
                        shadowRadius: 8,
                        elevation: 3,
                        backgroundColor: 'transparent',
                      }}
                      onPress={() => handleNavigate(item.screen)}
                      accessibilityLabel={item.label}
                      activeOpacity={0.75}
                    >
                      <BlurView
                        intensity={Platform.OS === 'ios' ? 56 : 20} // lighter nested blur
                        tint={isDark ? 'dark' : 'light'}
                        style={{
                          borderRadius: 14,
                          overflow: 'hidden',
                          borderWidth: 1,
                          borderColor: isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.15)' : 'rgba(255,255,255,0.5)',
                          backgroundColor: 'transparent',
                        }}
                      >
                        <LinearGradient
                          colors={
                            isDark
                              ? ['rgba(255,255,255,0.08)', 'rgba(255,255,255,0.04)']
                              : ['rgba(255,255,255,0.55)', 'rgba(255,255,255,0.25)']
                          }
                          start={{ x: 0, y: 0 }}
                          end={{ x: 0, y: 1 }}
                          style={{
                            flexDirection: 'row',
                            alignItems: 'center',
                            paddingVertical: spacing.md,
                            paddingHorizontal: spacing.sm,
                            minHeight: 56,
                          }}
                        >
                          <Feather name={item.icon as any} size={20} color={colors.text} style={styles.menuIcon} />
                          <Text style={[styles.menuLabel, { color: colors.text }]}>{item.label}</Text>
                          <Feather name="chevron-right" size={18} color={colors.muted ?? 'rgba(0,0,0,0.4)'} />
                        </LinearGradient>
                      </BlurView>
                    </TouchableOpacity>
                  ))}
                </View>

                {/* Footer */}
                <View style={styles.footer}>
                  <Text style={[styles.footerText, { color: colors.muted }]}>Music App v1.0
by Saw K Za</Text>
                </View>
              </Animated.View>
            </SafeAreaView>
          </LinearGradient>
        </BlurView>

        {/* Thin glass border edge */}
        <View
          pointerEvents="none"
          style={[
            styles.glassEdge,
            { borderRightColor: isDark ? 'rgba(255,255,255,0.06)' : 'rgba(0,0,0,0.06)' },
          ]}
        />
      </Animated.View>
    </Animated.View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    ...StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject,
  },
  overlay: {
    ...StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject,
  },

  // Drawer shell
  drawer: {
    position: 'absolute',
    top: 0,
    overflow: 'hidden',
    borderTopRightRadius: 28,
    borderBottomRightRadius: 28,
    shadowColor: '#000',
    shadowOffset: { width: 6, height: 10 },
    shadowOpacity: 0.18,
    shadowRadius: 30,
    elevation: 30,
    backgroundColor: 'transparent',
  },

  blurContainer: {
    flex: 1,
    overflow: 'hidden',
    borderTopRightRadius: 28,
    borderBottomRightRadius: 28,
  },

  gradientOverlay: { flex: 1 },
  safe: { flex: 1 },

  innerContent: {
    flex: 1,
    paddingHorizontal: spacing.md * 1.5,
    paddingTop: spacing.md * 1.5,
    paddingBottom: spacing.md,
    overflow: 'hidden',
  },

  header: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'space-between',
    paddingHorizontal: spacing.md,
    paddingBottom: spacing.sm,
    marginBottom: spacing.sm,
  },
  headerTitle: {
    fontSize: 24,
    fontWeight: '900',
    letterSpacing: 0.2,
    textShadowColor: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.08)',
    textShadowOffset: { width: 0, height: 1 },
    textShadowRadius: 6,
  },
  closeButton: {
    padding: spacing.sm,
    borderRadius: 14,
    backgroundColor: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.03)',
  },

  menuItems: { flex: 1, paddingTop: spacing.sm },
  menuItem: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    paddingVertical: spacing.md,
    paddingHorizontal: spacing.sm,
    marginBottom: spacing.sm,
    borderRadius: 14,
    borderWidth: 1,
    minHeight: 56,
    shadowColor: '#000',
    shadowOffset: { width: 0, height: 3 },
    shadowOpacity: 0.06,
    shadowRadius: 8,
    elevation: 2,
    backgroundColor: 'transparent',
  },
  menuIcon: { marginRight: spacing.md, opacity: 0.95 },
  menuLabel: { fontSize: 16, fontWeight: '700', flex: 1 },

  footer: {
    paddingVertical: spacing.md,
    alignItems: 'center',
    borderTopWidth: 1,
    borderTopColor: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.03)',
    marginTop: spacing.sm,
  },
  footerText: { fontSize: 12, opacity: 0.8, letterSpacing: 0.2 },

  glassEdge: {
    position: 'absolute',
    top: 0,
    bottom: 0,
    right: -1,
    width: 2,
    borderRightWidth: 1,
    opacity: 0.95,
    backgroundColor: 'transparent',
    shadowColor: '#fff',
    shadowOffset: { width: -1, height: 0 },
    shadowOpacity: 0.025,
    shadowRadius: 6,
    elevation: 0,
  },
});

export default GlassDrawer;
```

Why this fixes your issues
- Unresponsive after navigating back: the drawer fully unmounts when closed (mounted=false), and the top container has pointerEvents set based on isOpen. Nothing remains to intercept touches.
- Lag/white ghost: lower blur intensity (especially nested Blurs), and slightly less opaque light gradient reduce the bright, heavy look and improve performance.

What not to change
- Don’t touch your navigation logic, stack structure, or other screens.
- Keep HomeScreen importing GlassDrawer from src/components/GlassDrawer.
- Don’t rename files or add dependencies.

Test steps
1) Save the file and restart Expo (recommended):
- npx expo start --clear
2) Open drawer → tap Profile → back to Home.
3) Open drawer again → all items and the Home list should respond.
4) Try multiple open/close cycles. The lag and white halo should be noticeably reduced.

If the issue persists
- Confirm the file path matches your import: src/components/GlassDrawer.tsx.
- Make sure HomeScreen doesn’t have any leftover inline drawer overlay layers.
- If you see any errors, paste them here. I can adjust the timing or pointerEvents further.

You’re seeing a bright vertical band because the drawer’s right-edge highlight and shadows are bleeding into the dim overlay area. It looks like a “second drawer,” but it’s actually the drawer’s glassEdge highlight and outer elevation/shadow projecting into the overlay on Android.

Fix (safe and minimal):
- Remove the glassEdge highlight (or make it fully transparent).
- Slightly overlap the overlay over the drawer’s right edge to hide any 1px seam.
- Tone down shadows so nothing bleeds to the right.

Paste this updated file to replace your GlassDrawer. It keeps your logic and UI, only adjusts the edge/shadow and overlay.

